(Plan 310 task 6 - printing a whole thing walks its fields in definition
 order and recurses into the things they hold (§7), and `is` between two of
 the same thing compares those same fields at the same depth (§8). Both are
 written out by the compiler: every field name is baked into the emitted
 program, so nothing is read from a descriptor and nothing is allocated.

 The point's manifest member proves a function member takes no part in
 either. It is the type's API, not its state, so it is neither printed nor
 compared.

 The stamp carries the three remaining shapes of field - a quoted multi-word
 name, a float, and a boolean - so it proves each prints as it does anywhere
 else, with a multi-word name printed in the quotes it is written with.

 Acceptance: the twelve lines in the .expected, in that order.)

A thing called point has
  a function called 'placed at',
  a number called x is 0,
  a number called y is 0.

A thing called segment has
  a point called start,
  a point called end.

A thing called stamp has
  a number called 'day sent' is 25,
  a float called 'cost in pounds' is 1.5,
  a boolean called 'first class' is true.

To do the point's 'placed at', with a number called x and a number called y.
  a point called plotted.
  Set plotted's x to x.
  Set plotted's y to y.
  Return a point, plotted.

a point called origin.
Set origin's x to 5.
Print origin.

a segment called span.
Set span's end's y to 2.
Print span.
Print span's start.
Print "the span runs {span}".
Print "it starts at {span's start}".

a stamp called posted.
Print posted.

The corner is a point's 'placed at' with 3 and 4.
Print corner.

a point called marker.
Set marker's x to 5.
If origin is marker then,
    Print "the marker is where the origin is".
Set marker's y to 9.
If origin is marker then,
    Print "SHOULD NOT PRINT".
If origin is not marker then,
    Print "the marker has moved off the origin".

a segment called 'the detour'.
Set 'the detour''s end's y to 2.
If span is 'the detour' then,
    Print "the detour runs the same way".

a stamp called 'the reply stamp'.
If posted is 'the reply stamp' then,
    Print "two fresh stamps match".
Set 'the reply stamp''s 'cost in pounds' to 2.0.
If posted is 'the reply stamp' then,
    Print "SHOULD NOT PRINT".
Print "done".
